            <ArticleTitle>[Emergency coronary artery bypass grafting in a chronic hemodialysis patient: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1119-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Emergency coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) was performed on a 48-year-old male with a long-term hemodialysis history. Following the operation, the patient developed acute elevation of potassium. We applied hemodialysis and obtained beneficial beneficial results. No remarkable change on hemodynamics and coagulant system was observed. Hemodialysis should be recommended on an acute phase for the patients of good cardiac function with less bleeding during the operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
